Well, cats tend to get stuck in and under
things, so anything (say, a suit of armor)
capable of sheltering a cat might well be
an opportunity for kitty to disappear from
sight and start filling the message lines
with pitiful mews for help.

As for Bowser, well, dogs' most famous
unwanted behavior seems to be digging
up the lawn or garden, so perhaps:

1) A dog falling into a pit has a small
chance to start digging, and if not
rescued or self-released from the trap
sufficiently soon, might dig through and
fall to the next level.

2) A Dog left unaccosted by monsters and
unleased, undisplaced, and otherwise
bored, might pass the time by digging a
pit. Just naturally, the PC wouldn't see
the pit, Bowser being neglected at the
time and all.

Losing Bowser in some distant room for a long
period could lead to real problems, like a
room entirely filled with pits by the time the
PC goes to explore it.

Dogs' next most famous misbehavior is
probably chewing, so there might be some
chance of Phideaux munching leather goods
into disrepair before the PC can even get
to those objects, or chewing through a
leash.

